WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:17.817
Unit thirteen: B2 First: Reading Parts 5 to 7. Today you will answer multiple-choice, gapped-text and matching questions.

4
00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.886
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:25.031
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.873
Inference.

7
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.765
Inference means an idea understood from clues.

8
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.630
Make an inference.

9
00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:35.544
Your turn. Say: Inference.

10
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.459
Inference.

11
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:41.322
Gapped text.

12
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:45.129
Gapped text means a text with removed sentences.

13
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.472
Part 6 is a gapped text.

14
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:50.817
Your turn. Say: Gapped text.

15
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.912
Gapped text.

16
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.046
Multiple matching.

17
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.187
Multiple matching means matching statements with sections.

18
00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:03.899
Part 7 is multiple matching.

19
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:07.217
Your turn. Say: Multiple matching.

20
00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.288
Multiple matching.

21
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:12.923
Reference.

22
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.381
Reference means a word that points back.

23
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:18.913
The pronoun is a reference.

24
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:21.960
Your turn. Say: Reference.

25
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.673
Reference.

26
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:27.511
Paraphrase.

27
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:31.526
Paraphrase means the same idea in other words.

28
00:01:32.117 --> 00:01:33.965
The question is a paraphrase.

29
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.318
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

30
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.330
Paraphrase.

31
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.096
Main point.

32
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:46.454
Main point means the most important idea.

33
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.318
Find the main point.

34
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:51.383
Your turn. Say: Main point.

35
00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.501
Main point.

36
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.181
Attitude.

37
00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:00.485
Attitude means how someone feels.

38
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:03.118
The writer's attitude is positive.

39
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:06.439
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

40
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.231
Attitude.

41
00:02:10.983 --> 00:02:11.996
Eliminate.

42
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:15.482
Eliminate means to remove wrong options.

43
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:18.187
Eliminate two options first.

44
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:21.273
Your turn. Say: Eliminate.

45
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.030
Eliminate.

46
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:29.844
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:34.064
Visal, what do Parts 5, 6 and 7 test?

48
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:49.276
Part 5 is a long text with multiple-choice questions on detail, opinion and attitude. Part 6 asks you to put missing sentences back into a text. Part 7 asks you to match statements to sections or texts.

49
00:02:50.383 --> 00:02:52.093
How do I do Part 6?

50
00:02:53.183 --> 00:03:04.903
Read the text around each gap and look for links such as pronouns, linking words and repeated nouns. Each sentence must connect both before and after the gap.

51
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:07.471
How do I do Part 7?

52
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:17.888
Read the statements first and underline key ideas. Then scan the sections for paraphrases of those ideas, not for the same words.

53
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.789
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.437
Grammar focus: Strategy: links, paraphrase, evidence.

55
00:03:25.737 --> 00:03:26.936
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.472
The pronoun 'this' refers back to the idea in the sentence before.

57
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:36.577
The statement says 'costly'; the text says 'expensive to maintain'.

58
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:44.595
Look for links between sentences, expect paraphrase between questions and text, and find evidence for every answer.

59
00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.105
Be careful! Don't say: I match by the same words.

60
00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.217
Say: I match by meaning.

61
00:03:53.517 --> 00:03:55.029
Look for paraphrase.

62
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:58.312
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.565
A Gapped Text.

64
00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:03.538
Nita reads an article about a young inventor.

65
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:06.904
One missing sentence begins with This.

66
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.109
She looks at the sentence before the gap.

67
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.272
It describes a new machine, so This refers to the machine.

68
00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:18.300
She chooses the sentence that connects both sides.

69
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.680
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:24.517 --> 00:04:26.423
Part 6 is a blank text.

71
00:04:26.723 --> 00:04:30.632
A, table only. B, gapped. C, poem.

72
00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.841
The answer is B: gapped.

73
00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:38.693
Pronouns help you find blank.

74
00:04:38.993 --> 00:04:42.716
A, spelling. B, dates. C, links.

75
00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.464
The answer is C: links.

76
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:52.150
In Part 7 statements are matched with blank.

77
00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:56.661
A, sections or texts. B, pictures. C, songs.

78
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.047
The answer is A: sections or texts.

79
00:05:04.183 --> 00:05:06.810
The text uses a blank of the statement words.

80
00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.670
A, title. B, paraphrase. C, copy.

81
00:05:14.233 --> 00:05:16.337
The answer is B: paraphrase.

82
00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.912
What does 'This' refer to in Nita's gap?

83
00:05:20.212 --> 00:05:23.727
A, the day. B, the weather. C, the machine.

84
00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.626
The answer is C: the machine.

85
00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:34.240
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:37.094
How do you do a gapped-text task?

87
00:05:45.883 --> 00:05:47.349
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.649 --> 00:06:03.655
I read the text around the gap and look for links such as pronouns, linking words and repeated nouns. I choose the sentence that connects with both the part before and the part after. Then I check that the whole text makes sense.

89
00:06:03.955 --> 00:06:06.094
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:13.188
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: links, paraphrase, evidence.

91
00:06:13.488 --> 00:06:18.045
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

92
00:06:18.345 --> 00:06:21.171
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:21.471 --> 00:06:24.576
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

